From b9d5e61c5562ede06625f9d738072f5734fc8909 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mathias Heider <mathias.heider@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 02:44:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Load a .env locally so the agent runs outside a Space

The Space injects its secrets into the environment; a local checkout has
nothing doing that, so a clone failed with a bare 'Postgres config
incomplete' (or a psycopg traceback in the UI) even with a .env sitting next
to app.py -- nothing ever read that file.

- envfile.py: stdlib-only .env loader. Never overrides a variable already
  present in the environment -- present includes present-and-empty, so a Space
  secret blanked on purpose is not refilled from a file. Handles the ways a
  .env actually arrives on Windows: .env.txt, UTF-16 with and without a BOM,
  BOMs, CRLF, 'export ' prefixes, quoted values, inline comments. Inside
  double quotes only \" and \\ are escapes, so C:\temp\notes survives.
  Diagnostics never quote a value: 'python envfile.py' prints a masked
  self-check that is safe to paste into a chat, and masking is an allow-list
  so DB_HOST/DB_USER/DB_NAME cannot leak through it.
- local_bootstrap.py: builds an empty schema on a local Postgres so a dev
  never needs the shared RDS credentials. It decides 'local' by asking the
  server where it is (host(inet_server_addr())), not by trusting the hostname
  -- an SSH tunnel on localhost:5433, a hosts-file entry and a DATABASE_URL
  pointing at RDS are all refused. DATABASE_URL also drives the check itself,
  because it is what pg_mirror connects through; checking DB_* while writing
  through DATABASE_URL would guard the wrong server.
- agent/config.py: loads it; missing_db_vars()/setup_hint(), and an
  unparseable DATABASE_URL counts as missing rather than 'unreachable'.
- agent/ui_common.py: an unconfigured DB says what is missing and where it
  goes, instead of a psycopg traceback.
- extraction.py / pdf_crawler.py: same preamble -- both read the environment
  at import time, so GEMINI_MODEL and S2_API_KEY were missed by any entry
  point that imported them before the agent package.
- .dockerignore: Dockerfile does COPY . /app, and a developer .env would
  otherwise be baked into the image and applied at runtime on the Space.
- test_envfile.py: 27 regression tests, one per defect found in review.
- .env.example, LOCAL_SETUP.md, README section, .gitignore.

Verified: 27/27 envfile regression tests; full test_e2e.py cycle green
against a local Postgres configured only by a .env; AppTest shows the
actionable error with no config and boots clean with one; with no .env and
secrets in the environment the app behaves exactly as it does on HF, and no
longer logs a warning telling the operator to create a .env.
